mptcp-bpf-weight-rr (1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Screen candidates on send-buffer availability before the smooth weighted
    round-robin bookkeeping, not after it. The winner's current-weight was
    debited by total_weight and the pick was then discarded if its send buffer
    was full -- and the heavy endpoint is exactly the one whose buffer fills,
    since it carries the traffic, so it burned its turns without sending and
    the light endpoints collected the sends. Weights 250/10/10 put 52-71% on
    the heavy WAN instead of the expected ~96%; it now measures ~92%.

 -- Yannick Chabanois <contact@openmptcprouter.com>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

mptcp-bpf-weight-rr (1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging of the bpf_weight_rr MPTCP scheduler,
    split out of the mptcp-bpf-weight source package into its own
    source package so it can be installed/versioned independently of
    the single-winner mptcp-bpf-weight scheduler. Same BPF program and
    systemd unit as when it was bundled there; still shares the
    endpoint_weights/weight_remote_id BPF maps and the
    mptcp-weight-manager CLI (packaged by mptcp-bpf-weight) with it.

 -- Yannick Chabanois <contact@openmptcprouter.com>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000
